# widgets1.mtb

note
note What value are you assuming for the 
note population proportion of defectives?
set 'terminal' c63;
nobs=1.
copy c63 k63
note
note How many samples do you want to simulate?
set 'terminal' c64;
nobs=1.
copy c64 k64
note
note How many widgets are to be in each sample?
set 'terminal' c65;
nobs=1.
copy c65 k65
note
note Please wait.
note
rand k64 c72;
bino k65 k63.
let c71=c72/k65
name c72 'num def'
name c71 'p-hat'
note
note
note If you want to analyze the results of the simulation more fully,
note the numbers of defectives in each sample are in c72
note and the sample proportions of defectives are in c71.
note
note
note Here are summary statistics and visual displays for the
note distribution of sample numbers of defectives:
tally c72
desc c72
dotp c72
hist c72
note
note Do you want to count the number of sample defectives
note falling in a certain interval?  Enter how many such counts
note would like to do.  (Enter 0 if none.)
set 'terminal' c66;
nobs=1.
copy c66 k66
exec 'count\count1.mtb' k66
note
end

